---
const technologies = [
  {
    name: "AWS",
    icon: "/tech-icons/aws.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "Terraform",
    icon: "/tech-icons/terraform.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "Docker",
    icon: "/tech-icons/docker.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "Python",
    icon: "/tech-icons/python.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "PostgreSQL",
    icon: "/tech-icons/postgresql.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "Airflow",
    icon: "/tech-icons/airflow.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "Spark",
    icon: "/tech-icons/spark.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "Databricks",
    icon: "/tech-icons/databricks.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "React",
    icon: "/tech-icons/react.svg",
  },
  {
    name: "TypeScript",
    icon: "/tech-icons/typescript.svg",
  },
];
---

<section id="technologies" class="py-32">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 max-w-prose">
    <p class="text-3xl mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      Experienced <span
        class="font-bold underline decoration-4 decoration-accent underline-offset-8"
        >software engineer</span
      > helping businesses build scalable, <span
        class="font-bold underline decoration-4 decoration-accent underline-offset-8"
        >data-heavy</span
      > applications that deliver <span
        class="font-bold underline decoration-4 decoration-accent underline-offset-8"
        >results</span
      >.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col lg:!flex-row mt-64">
    <div class="w-full lg:!w-1/2 flex flex-col justify-center gap-4 px-8">
      <h2
        class="text-3xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-center max-w-prose mx-auto pb-8"
      >
        Scalable Data Architectures
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-prose mx-auto font-serif">
        I help design, build, and maintain scalable data architectures based on
        <span class="font-bold"
          >best-in-class, well-established technologies</span
        >.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-prose mx-auto font-serif">
        Usually, I design architectures on <span class="font-bold">AWS</span> where
        I am certified as Solutions Architect Professional since 2021, but have worked
        with Azure and Kubernetes-based deployments as well.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-prose mx-auto font-serif">
        My data architectures rely on a mix of file storage systems like <span
          class="font-bold">S3</span
        > and <span class="font-bold">Delta Lake</span>, SQL databases like <span
          class="font-bold">PostgreSQL</span
        >, and NoSQL databases like <span class="font-bold">DynamoDB</span> or <span
          class="font-bold">Elasticsearch</span
        >, based on data volume and usage patterns.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-prose mx-auto font-serif">
        I like building backend systems in <span class="font-bold">Python</span
        >, data pipelines with
        <span class="font-bold">Spark</span> and <span class="font-bold"
          >Databricks</span
        >, and orchestrating workflows with <span class="font-bold"
          >Airflow</span
        >, but I'm always interested in learning about and adopting new
        technologies.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-prose mx-auto font-serif">
        To set up and evolve cloud architectures I implement <span
          class="font-bold">CI/CD pipelines</span
        > that rely on Infrastructure-as-Code tools like
        <span class="font-bold">CDK</span> or <span class="font-bold"
          >Terraform</span
        >.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-prose mx-auto font-serif pb-8">
        For user interfaces, I like to use the <span class="font-bold"
          >React/TypeScript/Next.js</span
        >
        ecosystem and also have some experience with newer frameworks like Astro.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="bg-tertiary rounded-l-2xl p-8 shadow-lg w-5/6 lg:!w-1/2 ml-auto"
    >
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 lg:!grid-cols-3 gap-6 justify-items-center">
        {
          technologies.map((tech) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center group">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 flex items-center justify-center mb-3 bg-secondary rounded-xl p-3 shadow-sm border border-gray-100 transition-all duration-200 group-hover:scale-110 group-hover:shadow-md">
                <img
                  src={tech.icon}
                  alt={tech.name}
                  class="w-full h-full object-contain"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </div>
              <span class="text-sm font-medium text-secondary text-center">
                {tech.name}
              </span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container mx-auto pt-64 px-4 md:px-6 max-w-prose">
    <p class="text-3xl mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      I focus on <span
        class="font-bold underline decoration-4 decoration-accent underline-offset-8"
        >reducing complexity</span
      >. Keeping it simple is a great way to deliver <span
        class="font-bold underline decoration-4 decoration-accent underline-offset-8"
      >
        maintainable software</span
      > while keeping a <span
        class="font-bold underline decoration-4 decoration-accent underline-offset-8"
        >high development speed</span
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
